### Basic usage: access req.log and res.log

Source: https://github.com/pinojs/pino-http/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/http-logger.md

Sets up a basic HTTP server with pino-http. The logger is called with req and res, making req.log and res.log available for logging within the request lifecycle.

```javascript
const http = require('http')
const logger = require('pino-http')()

http.createServer((req, res) => {
  logger(req, res)
  req.log.info('request handler started')
  res.log.info('response in scope, request still available too')
  res.end('hello world')
}).listen(3000)
```

